"text": "He was Glyndwr Michael, from Aberbargoed, a mining town in the valleys of South Wales. His father, a coal miner, took his own life when Glyndwr was fifteen. His mother died when he was thirty-one. He had worked odd jobs as a gardener and a labourer. Homeless, with no money and no family to turn to, he drifted to London.",
